From 7f0ee8f07cd70a795cea69f2bb5087f1a8b159d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giorgos Sarigiannidis <contact@gsarigiannidis.gr>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:29:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Add a base-anchored three-way merge model

Stock Meld diffs the result against each side and recomputes after every
edit, so an applied change just stops being a difference and a dismissed
one comes back. Instead, fix the changes once against the common
base and read each one's state from the result text: applied when the
text there equals that side (or both sides joined, or the magic wand's
word-level merge); only dismissals are stored, as the text they were
made against. Undo, typing and reopening a half-done file all follow.

The result is read as the base's unchanged runs in order with each run
of touching changes between them holding one of its known texts, so
look-alike lines cannot misplace a change; a base->result diff is the
fallback when an unchanged run itself was edited.

AnchoredMergeDiffer keeps Meld's own result<->side chunks for alignment
and re-tags them from the model: conflict, the usual change tags, or a
new 'resolved'. Nothing uses it yet; the merge view comes next.
